{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931274-mummy","id":931274,"title":"Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T04:53:46-07:00","id":931274,"title":"Mummy","content":"I just bought the PDF of Mummy the Curse and was wondering, Has anyone used one of the Arisen as an antagonist in a CofD game? It could get pretty creepy with the cultists and stuff. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T07:21:42-07:00","id":931333,"title":"","content":"You may want to check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/551708-a-mummy-and-5-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar\">this thread</a> for starters. It deals with a specific scenario, but serves to showcase some of the difficulties of pitting pretty much anything against the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:07:24-07:00","id":931397,"title":"","content":"Mummies make problematic antagonists. With their power and cult, they make great hidden villains... except that after all that time is when they are the <i>weakest</i>. But if you throw a Mummy at the characters to begin with, they'll get torn apart. It's hard making them recurring antagonists, too, since they are likely to forget you the next time or two they are awake.<br /> <br /> You are basically either running:<br /> 1. You encounter the freshly woken mummy, get you asses handed to you, and the mummy lets you live (for Reasons). Cue Villain Cliche regarding letting foes live.<br /> 2. You are actually fighting the Cult more than the mummy. The mummy then becomes a big mean &quot;end boss&quot; that finally gets woken up in time for a big confrontation. But then the mummy is barely capable of social interaction, so it looses a number of themes and just becomes a fight scene.<br /> 3. You deliberately play around the mummy as a mysterious NPC, acting mostly through their cult, but occasionally personally. You might even run the mummy as an ally, until they get woken up again, and are manipulated into thinking you are their enemy (see the Memory issue above).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:35:21-07:00","id":931409,"title":"","content":"I'm immensely more fond of &quot;you're part of an Arisen's cult and don't even know it, fighting their enemies, gathering relics, and competing with other cults.&quot; Trying to actually fight a mummy as anything other than anither mummy is suicidal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:55:58-07:00","id":931423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931274-mummy?p=931409#post931409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm immensely more fond of &quot;you're part of an Arisen's cult and don't even know it, fighting their enemies, gathering relics, and competing with other cults.&quot; Trying to actually fight a mummy as anything other than anither mummy is suicidal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>can</i> be done, if you know enough of their weaknesses and strengths, and employ non-ghost ephemerals and <i>lots</i> of fire. Filling their tomb with multiple, separate sections of napalm and motion triggers works pretty well from when they wake back up again, or come &quot;home&quot; to recharge. Eventually they'll forget you.<br /> <br /> Your friends are fire, distance, and proxies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:14:36-07:00","id":932261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931274-mummy?p=931423#post931423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your friends are fire, distance, and proxies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come on now. That applies to fighting pretty much every supernatural on Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T19:21:41-07:00","id":932324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931274-mummy?p=932261#post932261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Come on now. That applies to fighting pretty much every supernatural on Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. Werewolves, it's silver instead of fire. Mages, it's disposable Sleepers. Changelings is Cold Iron and random trolling. Sin-Eaters is... concrete, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:11:29-07:00","id":932406,"title":"","content":"I do not like <b>The Curse</b> setting ( to Egypt-centric for my <b>CoD</b> ) so when making 'mummy-like' antagonists I use Horror rules or make good Osirian Promethean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:28:16-07:00","id":934913,"title":"","content":"I did once and it turend in to an interesting situation where my players were uncovering parts of the mummies history until they were in a position to confront it about its memories. <br /> <br /> I won't lie I did not know the depth of the mummy system when I was doing it (they probably would have died if I strictly just used powers to smack them around) but I followed what I knew at the time and everyone seemed to enjoy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3141-shadow7045","name":"Shadow7045","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:30:39-07:00","id":934915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931274-mummy?p=932324#post932324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not quite. Werewolves, it's silver instead of fire. Mages, it's disposable Sleepers. Changelings is Cold Iron and random trolling. Sin-Eaters is... concrete, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those would still die to a firey explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}